    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nPlugin explicitly starts treesitter causing neovim to freeze\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.9.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. install treesitter syntax for js (doesn't matter if it's js/css or any other language)\r\n2. enable mini.files preview\r\n3. create following structure (use at least ~500kB minified js file) i.e.:\r\n```bash\r\nmkdir some-dir\r\ntouch some-dir/a.js some-dir/b.js some-dir/d.js\r\ncurl https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/angular2@2.0.0-beta.21/bundles/angular2-all.umd.min.js > some-dir/c-slow.js\r\n```\r\n4. browse this structure from `some-dir/a.js` to `some-dir/d.js` with `j`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should be possible to preview a file without starting treesitter / enabling syntax highlighting or decide whenever to show preview for specific file. \r\n\r\nThere are few options for current implementation\r\n\r\n1. `boolean` option to disable syntax highlighting globally for mini.files\r\n2. `function` option to disable preview completely per file (similarly how non text files work)\r\n3. `function` option to disable syntax highlighting per file\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nNeovim freezes when large minified file is previewed.\r\n\r\nIt is possible to use `MiniFilesBufferUpdate` to disable syntax and stop treesitter, but you will still experience little freeze first time you preview file (caused by already started treesitter).\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- current workaround\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"User\", {\r\n    group = vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\"mygroup\", { clear = true }),\r\n    pattern = \"MiniFilesBufferUpdate\",\r\n    callback = function(args)\r\n        local buffer = args.data.buf_id\r\n\r\n        vim.bo[buffer].syntax = nil\r\n        vim.treesitter.stop(buffer)\r\n    end,\r\n})\r\n``` ",
