            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I can partially reproduce: it doesn't exactly \"freezes\" (which I perceived as \"indefinitely stopped responding\"), but is being blocked for rendering lines.\r\n\r\nIt's same for me. Sorry for inaccurate word.\r\n\r\nAnother workaround could be shortening lines to length of `width_preview`, however this can easily break highlighted syntax.\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n-- Compute lines. Limit number of read lines to work better on large files.\r\nlocal has_lines, read_res = pcall(vim.fn.readfile, path, '', vim.o.lines)\r\n-- - Make sure that lines don't contain '\\n' (might happen in binary files).\r\nlocal lines = has_lines and vim.split(table.concat(read_res, '\\n'), '\\n') or {}\r\nfor i, line in pairs(lines) do\r\n  lines[i] = line:sub(1, opts.windows.width_preview)\r\nend\r\n```",
