            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> I'd probably not highlight if total size of lines is above certain threshold.\r\n\r\nThis is how I've fixed it for now with `MiniFilesBufferUpdate`.\r\n```lua\r\ncallback = function(args)\r\n    local bufnr = args.data.buf_id\r\n                                                                      \r\n    if vim.api.nvim_buf_is_loaded(bufnr) then\r\n        local lines = vim.api.nvim_buf_get_lines(bufnr, 0, -1, false)\r\n        for _, line in pairs(lines) do\r\n            if #line > 3000 then\r\n                vim.treesitter.stop(bufnr)\r\n                vim.bo[bufnr].syntax = nil\r\n                                                                      \r\n                break\r\n            end\r\n        end\r\n    end\r\nend,\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor me it would be optimal to run this check before starting treesitter / syntax highlighting.\r\n\r\nSomething like this would be enough\r\n```lua\r\n-- Add highlighting on Neovim>=0.8 which has stabilized API\r\nif vim.fn.has('nvim-0.8') == 1 and opts.windows.preview_syntax_start(buf_id, lines) then -- or just buf_id\r\n```",
